1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,265
The WenQuest learning platform is modeled on Canvas,

2
00:00:03,285 --> 00:00:05,460
with one codebase for the web and WeChat.

3
00:00:06,480 --> 00:00:09,310
Building a course starts with one sentence, for example:

4
00:00:09,330 --> 00:00:12,618
a sixteen-week physics course for first-year mechanical students.

5
00:00:13,088 --> 00:00:17,338
Behind it sits a whole AI faculty team: a librarian, a course designer,

6
00:00:17,358 --> 00:00:20,045
a lecturer, a question writer and a reviewer.

7
00:00:21,065 --> 00:00:22,874
Give it your materials, however messy.

8
00:00:22,894 --> 00:00:25,811
The AI sorts them and finds the main textbook and references,

9
00:00:26,281 --> 00:00:29,971
and the course lead asks about anything unclear, all at once.

10
00:00:30,991 --> 00:00:34,772
The AI acts like a course lead: it settles the students and goals,

11
00:00:34,792 --> 00:00:39,034
drafts the outline and a course design book, then writes lesson by lesson.

12
00:00:39,504 --> 00:00:42,029
You can change any step, and undo it.

13
00:00:43,049 --> 00:00:46,950
Slides are interactive web pages: page through them like PowerPoint,

14
00:00:46,970 --> 00:00:50,526
with animations, labs and 3D models working right on the page.

15
00:00:51,546 --> 00:00:53,634
Behind the courses are our own textbooks;

16
00:00:53,654 --> 00:00:57,079
each chapter lists its animations and labs up front, ready to open.

17
00:00:58,099 --> 00:01:01,834
What you get is a complete course. Teachers approve every lesson,

18
00:01:02,304 --> 00:01:05,152
and the school's course committee signs off before it goes live.

19
00:01:06,172 --> 00:01:09,494
Sign up free, and teachers are welcome to run courses here.
